Task 5.1: Screen-music Playwright proof (e2e/music.spec.ts, 5 tests)

What: An in-page audio probe (wraps createOscillator/createBufferSource)
counts synthesized nodes as the honest observable for 'music is
scheduling'. Proofs: no music before the first tap; one theme flows
across hash navigation; mute freezes the counter and persists across
reload; unmute resumes; bedtime swaps in a looping lullaby; music works
fully offline (synthesis needs no network).

Real bugs found and fixed while making it pass:
1. Settings fork: ParentScreen and Shell each ran usePetSave, so the
   panel's mute/bedtime toggles never reached the Shell's music hook.
   The old direct stopMusic() inside useSettings masked this and left
   the hook's playing state stale (silence that never resumed). Fix:
   Shell owns settings once and passes them to ParentScreen as props;
   useSettings no longer touches the audio engine (decideMusic owns the
   whole music lifecycle now).
2. Test timing: sparse themes (room/lullaby) only top up the 2s
   lookahead window every ~1s, so 400ms freeze-checks were too short;
   waits lengthened to 1200/1500ms with comments.

Verification: e2e/music.spec.ts 5/5; full e2e suite 27/27; units
208/208; pnpm check clean. Gates: strict TS, Biome, no UI added.
